{
  "introduction": {
    "text": "The Tenuta presidenziale di Castelporziano, commonly known as Castello, is one of Italy’s three presidential residences. Located 25 km from Rome, it serves as a historic estate, a presidential retreat, a natural reserve, and a venue for contemporary art. Its layered history, architectural features, and cultural programs make it a significant cultural and political landmark.",
    "sourceIds": ["wikipedia"]
  },
